            "For a hypothetical calendar, imagine buying on Monday and confirming international handover the following week. An international estimate measured from handover should not be counted from that earlier Monday. The example explains the clock, not a promised service speed. If timing is essential for an event, consider whether the full sequence has enough margin before ordering. A narrow estimated range is still not a guarantee against capacity changes, inspections or local delivery issues."
