      "opening": "Warehouse storage gives a UK buyer time to coordinate purchases, but it should have a purpose and an end date. Waiting without a plan can turn a convenient service into missed deadlines or unnecessary spending. Sugargoo's published storage guide distinguishes purchasing orders from resell and forwarding orders; its consolidation guide describes selecting received items and submitting a parcel. This article combines those workflows into a practical decision record. Current account information and service terms should resolve any difference with older public guidance.",
