            "For each item, mark QC as unchecked, clarification needed or accepted. Add an after-sales deadline where known and a next-action date. Keep unresolved items out of a final parcel. If you are waiting for a measurement, request it early enough to make a decision while the seller's terms still matter. The warehouse should not become a place where difficult choices are postponed until everything has to be shipped in a rush."
