            "List items needing rigid protection, items that could mark or crush softer goods and anything requiring a route-specific check. Keep detachable parts traceable to the relevant order. Decide whether retail packaging is necessary only after the item's QC and return decision is complete. Clear instructions should identify the actual item and the protection required. A vague instruction such as “make it as small as possible” can hide a trade-off you would not have accepted explicitly."
